<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!-- Loaded only while "[sbz] Fridge" (sbz.NeatStorageFridge, by seobongzu) is active (LoadFolders.xml).

       VFE Factory's belts pull only from a storage building that is a factory hopper, or whose Def carries
       Pipe System's FactoryHopperExtension with isfactoryHopper true (Building_Conveyor.TryPullFromDir; code
       read 28 Oct 2026). Factory machines use the same flag to find input hoppers (Process.InputFactoryHopperDetected).
       VFE Factory itself flags Vanilla Chemfuel Expanded's chemfuel tap this way. The corpse fridge is an
       Adaptive Storage Framework building, and that framework keeps stored items spawned on the fridge's cells,
       which is where the belt looks. docs/development/vfe-factory-conveyors.md has the full reading. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAddModExtension">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="sbz_CorpseFridge"]</xpath>
    <value>
      <li Class="PipeSystem.FactoryHopperExtension">
        <isfactoryHopper>true</isfactoryHopper>
      </li>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
